  "id": "interpersonal-perception",
  "term": "interpersonal perception",
  "definition": "Interpersonal perception is how one person sees and evaluates another person in an interaction, such as viewing a partner neutrally or negatively. In joint action, this social perception can shape how people coordinate, including how much they adjust their movements to each other and how well they act together.",
